@page "/projects/portfolio/arch"
@page "/projects/web-development/backend"

<div class="project-page page-content">
	<header class="project-header">
		<p class="eyebrow">Web Development</p>
		<h1>Backend</h1>
		<p class="tagline">Cloud-native .NET services, integration boundaries, and backend code that favors clarity.</p>
	</header>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Professional Backend Experience</h2>
		<p>
			My resume centers on C#, .NET, ASP.NET Core, RESTful APIs, SQL Server, Azure, data modeling, and service-layer design. Across roles, I have built backend logic, data access layers, computational engines, generated-data scaffolding layers, Azure Functions prototypes, and APIs behind Angular and Blazor interfaces.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Repo Evidence</h2>
		<div class="project-grid">
			<article>
				<h3>ASP.NET Core</h3>
				<p>The portfolio app uses ASP.NET Core hosting, Razor Pages, Blazor Server, static files, routing, authentication, and authorization middleware.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>Microsoft Identity</h3>
				<p>The web app is configured with Microsoft.Identity.Web and Microsoft Identity UI for Azure AD sign-in flows.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>Minimal API</h3>
				<p>The Bible API project exposes compact HTTP endpoints for health checks, Bible metadata, recommended translations, and passage retrieval.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3>Typed Integration Client</h3>
				<p>The YouVersion client wraps HTTP calls, request headers, response parsing, error translation, and normalized response models.</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Backend Habits</h2>
		<ul class="project-list">
			<li>Validate inputs at the HTTP boundary before calling downstream services.</li>
			<li>Normalize external API responses into local response models.</li>
			<li>Make missing configuration fail clearly with actionable messages.</li>
			<li>Document local run, test URLs, deployment commands, secrets, and log inspection.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</div>
